QuestGuidance.Register("en",202,{
[6433]="7004C414\n1\tFind Dinodas in the Cobwebbed Wing of the Haunted Burrow\030Find Dinodas in the Creeping Wing of the Haunted Burrow\030Find Dinodas in the Basement of the Haunted Burrow\030Find Dinodas in the Attic of the Haunted Burrow\tDinodas can be found within the four wings of the Haunted Burrow. This quest requires access to the Haunted Burrow, which is available by completing the quest chain that begins with 'A Cellar Door Appears.'\n2\tTalk to Dinodas near the Party Tree\tDinodas is outside the Haunted Burrow, near the Party Tree.\n",
[6434]="7004C413\n1\tEncourage bashful festival-goers to dance (total: 5)\tBashful festival-goers can be found around the Party Tree.\n2\tTalk to Esmeralda Boffin near the Party Tree\tEsmeralda Boffin is near the dance contest stage by the Party Tree.\n3\tUse the time to creatively express yourself\tEsmeralda Boffin is near the dance contest stage by the Party Tree.\n4\tTalk to Esmeralda Boffin near the Party Tree\tEsmeralda Boffin is near the dance contest stage by the Party Tree.\n",
[6435]="7004C386\n1\tDinodas heard something scary to the north-west and dropped his pack in the Bindbole Wood, and asked you to retrieve it for him.\t\n2\tTalk to the spectral vision\tA spectral vision has appeared in the Bindbole Wood.\n3\tReturn his dropped pack to Dinodas Boffin in the Bindbole Wood\tDinodas Boffin is to the south-east, in the Bindbole Wood.\n4\tTalk to Bingo in the Bindbole Wood\tBingo Boffin is in the Bindbole Wood, near his cousin Dinodas.\n",
[6436]="7004C381\n1\tHelp Prisca Boffin with 'Scary Dreams'\030Help Camellia Boffin with 'Boffin for Apples'\030Help Esmeralda Boffin with 'Fear Not To Dance!'\030Help Dinodas Boffin with 'Dinodas Does Not'\tBingo's cousin Prisca and her children can be found enjoying the various activities of the Harvest Festival near the Party Tree.\n2\tTalk to Bingo near the Party Tree\tBingo is near the Party Tree, waiting to hear how his cousins are enjoying the Harvest Festival.\n3\tHelp Bingo Boffin with 'A Little Spooky Research'\tBingo is near the Party Tree, in Hobbiton.\n4\tHelp Bingo Boffin with 'A Night for Ghost Stories'\tBingo is near the Party Tree in Hobbiton.\n5\tHelp Dinodas Boffin with 'Frightened Beyond Disbelief'\tDinodas Boffin is in the Bindbole Wood, in the Shire.\n6\tHelp Bingo Boffin with 'An Autumnal Mystery'\tBingo Boffin is in the Bindbole Wood, in the Shire.\n7\tTalk to Bingo near the Party Tree\tBingo said he would meet you back near the Party Tree, in Hobbiton.\n",
[6437]="7004C38F\n1\tFind Berilac Boffin somewhere on the Hill\tBerilac is probably sleeping among the bushes that line the road that climbs up to the Party Tree.\n2\tTalk to the costumed hobbit\tYou found Berilac Boffin, sound asleep by the side of the road. A hobbit wearing a scary costume prepares to scare the sleeping Boffin.\n3\tWake up Berilac Boffin\tBerilac is sleeping by the road that leads up to the Party Tree.\n4\tTalk to Berilac Boffin on the Hill\tYou have awoken Berilac Boffin for the Harvest Festival.\n5\tTalk to Prisca Boffin near the Party Tree\tPrisca Boffin is by the Party Tree.\n",
[6438]="700129D0\n1\tPeer into the Reflecting Pool and revisit 'The Eye of Angmar'\tThe Reflecting Pool on Tinnudir will allow you to revisit 'The Eye of Angmar.' A Sage of Eriador has challenged you to revisit your assault on Barad Tironn by using the Reflecting Pool on Tinnudir.\n2\tTalk to Maleniel\tA Sage of Eriador is by the Reflecting Pool on Tinnudir. A Sage of Eriador on Tinnudir is waiting to discuss what you have learned from revisiting your experience seeking the palantír within Barad Tironn.\n",
[6439]="700129D1\n1\tPeer into the Reflecting Pool and revisit 'Barad Tironn'\tThe Reflecting Pool on Tinnudir will allow you to revisit 'Barad Tironn.' A Sage of Eriador has challenged you to revisit your second assault on Barad Tironn by using the Reflecting Pool on Tinnudir.\n2\tTalk to Maleniel\tA Sage of Eriador is by the Reflecting Pool on Tinnudir. A Sage of Eriador on Tinnudir is waiting to discuss what you have learned from revisiting your second assault on Barad Tironn, seeking Laerdan.\n",
[6440]="700129D4\n1\tPeer into the Reflecting Pool and revisit 'Laerdan's Escape'\tThe Reflecting Pool in Aughaire will allow you to revisit 'Laerdan's Escape.' A Sage of Eriador has challenged you to revisit your experience freeing Laerdan from Sammath Baul by using the Reflecting Pool in Aughaire.\n2\tTalk to Rostellen\tA Sage of Eriador is by the Reflecting Pool in Aughaire. A Sage of Eriador in Aughaire is waiting to discuss what you have learned from revisiting your experience freeing Laerdan from Sammath Baul.\n",
[6441]="700129D5\n1\tPeer into the Reflecting Pool and revisit 'Weapons of the Enemy'\tThe Reflecting Pool in Aughaire will allow you to revisit 'Weapons of the Enemy.' A Sage of Eriador has challenged you to revisit your experience seeking Narchuil within Barad Dúrgul by using the Reflecting Pool in Aughaire.\n2\tTalk to Rostellen\tA Sage of Eriador is by the Reflecting Pool in Aughaire. A Sage of Eriador in Aughaire is waiting to discuss what you have learned from revisiting your experience seeking Narchuil within the fastness of Barad Dúrgul.\n",
[6442]="700129CD\n1\tPeer into the Reflecting Pool and revisit 'The Path of Aearil'\tThe Reflecting Pool in Sûri-kylä will allow you to revisit 'The Path of Aearil.' A Sage of Eriador has challenged you to revisit your experience seeking the second half of Narchuil in Forochel by using the Reflecting Pool in Sûri-kylä.\n2\tTalk to Maedbrennil\tA Sage of Eriador is by the Reflecting Pool in Sûri-kylä. A Sage of Eriador in Sûri-kylä is waiting to discuss what you have learned from revisiting your experience seeking the second half of Narchuil in Forochel.\n",
[6443]="700129D6\n1\tPeer into the Reflecting Pool and revisit 'The Heraldry of Lindon'\tThe Reflecting Pool in Aughaire will allow you to revisit 'The Heraldry of Lindon.' A Sage of Eriador has challenged you to revisit your experience seeking the breastplate of Laerdan within Dolendath by using the Reflecting Pool in Aughaire.\n2\tTalk to Rostellen\tA Sage of Eriador is by the Reflecting Pool in Aughaire. A Sage of Eriador in Aughaire is waiting to discuss what you have learned from revisiting your experience seeking the breastplate of Laerdan within Dolendath.\n",
[6444]="700129CE\n1\tPeer into the Reflecting Pool and revisit 'Skin of Bregmor'\tThe Reflecting Pool in Sûri-kylä will allow you to revisit 'Skin of Bregmor.' A Sage of Eriador has challenged you to revisit your experience seeking the hide of the Dragon of Forochel by using the Reflecting Pool in Sûri-kylä.\n2\tTalk to Maedbrennil\tA Sage of Eriador is by the Reflecting Pool in Sûri-kylä. A Sage of Eriador in Sûri-kylä is waiting to discuss what you have learned from revisiting your experience seeking the hide of the Dragon of Forochel.\n",
[6445]="700129B1\n1\tPeer into the Reflecting Pool and revisit 'The Doom of the North'\tThe Reflecting Pool in Rivendell will allow you to revisit 'The Doom of the North.' A Sage of Eriador has challenged you to revisit your experience seeking to upset Amarthiel's plans for the ring-forges of Mirobel by using the Reflecting Pool in Rivendell.\n2\tTalk to Taidbes\tA Sage of Eriador is by the Reflecting Pool in Rivendell. A Sage of Eriador in Rivendell is waiting to discuss what you have learned from revisiting your experience seeking to stop Amarthiel's plans for the Ring-forges of Mirobel.\n",
[6446]="70022FE0\n1\tPeer into the Reflecting Pool and revisit 'One Hope Remains'\tThe Reflecting Pool in Rivendell will allow you to revisit 'One Hope Remains.' A Sage of Eriador has challenged you to revisit your experience aiding Narmeleth in the destruction of Narchuil and Mordrambor.\n2\tTalk to the Sage of Eriador\tA Sage of Eriador is by the Reflecting Pool in Rivendell. A Sage of Eriador in Rivendell is waiting to discuss what you have learned from revisiting your experience aiding Narmeleth in the destruction of Narchuil and Mordrambor.\n",
[6447]="700129B4\n1\tPeer into the Reflecting Pool and revisit 'The Unmarked Trail'\tThe Reflecting Pool in Rivendell will allow you to revisit 'The Unmarked Trail.' A Sage of Eriador has challenged you to revisit your experience with Legolas by using the Reflecting Pool in Rivendell.\n2\tTalk to Taidbes\tA Sage of Eriador is by the Reflecting Pool in Rivendell. A Sage of Eriador in Rivendell is waiting to discuss what you have learned from revisiting your experience with Legolas in the Gladdalf.\n",
[6448]="700129B2\n1\tPeer into the Reflecting Pool and revisit 'The Last Refuge'\tThe Reflecting Pool in Rivendell will allow you to revisit 'The Last Refuge.' A Sage of Eriador has challenged you to revisit your experience with Gimli by using the Reflecting Pool in Rivendell.\n2\tTalk to Taidbes\tA Sage of Eriador is by the Reflecting Pool in Rivendell. A Sage of Eriador in Rivendell is waiting to discuss what you have learned from revisiting your experience with Gimli in the pass of Gabilazan.\n",
[6449]="700129B3\n1\tPeer into the Reflecting Pool and revisit 'Fire and Ice'\tThe Reflecting Pool in Rivendell will allow you to revisit 'Fire and Ice.' A Sage of Eriador has challenged you to revisit your experience deep within the treasury of Helegrod by using the Reflecting Pool in Rivendell.\n2\tTalk to Taidbes\tA Sage of Eriador is by the Reflecting Pool in Rivendell. A Sage of Eriador in Rivendell is waiting to discuss what you have learned from revisiting your experience within the treasury of Helegrod.\n",
[6450]="700129D7\n1\tPeer into the Reflecting Pool and revisit 'The Gates of Carn Dûm'\tThe Reflecting Pool in Aughaire will allow you to revisit 'The Gates of Carn Dûm.' A Sage of Eriador has challenged you to revisit your experience with Lorniel by using the Reflecting Pool in Aughaire.\n2\tTalk to Rostellen\tA Sage of Eriador is by the Reflecting Pool in Aughaire. A Sage of Eriador in Aughaire is waiting to discuss what you have learned from revisiting your experience with Lorniel at the gates of Carn Dûm.\n",
[6451]="700129D8\n1\tPeer into the Reflecting Pool and revisit 'Mordirith's Fall'\tThe Reflecting Pool in Aughaire will allow you to revisit 'Mordirith's Fall.' A Sage of Eriador has challenged you to revisit your experience with Golodir by using the Reflecting Pool in Aughaire.\n2\tTalk to Rostellen\tA Sage of Eriador is by the Reflecting Pool in Aughaire. A Sage of Eriador in Aughaire is waiting to discuss what you have learned from revisiting your experience with Golodir in the depths of Carn Dûm.\n",
[6452]="7004E17F\n1\tTalk to Angelica Boffin by the ponies in Wistmead\030Talk to Berilac Boffin by the edge of the maze in Wistmead\tAngelica and Berilac Boffin are somewhere in the Harvest Festival field of Wistmead.\n2\tTalk to Camellia Boffin by the tables in Wistmead\tCamellia Boffin is by a number of dining tables in Wistmead, helping to serve snacks to hungry patrons.\n3\tPick up a spider pie in Wistmead and carry it to Camellia Boffin\tCamellia asked you to pick up a pie from across the field in Wistmead and carry it back to her. She claimed that hungry hobbits would not bother you if you let them see the pie-filling, which has been made to look like spiders and creepy-crawlies.\n4\tTalk to Griffo Boffin in Wistmead\tGriffo Boffin is by the tables in Wistmead, looking unhappily at the spider-filled pies.\n5\tFind Marigold Boffin by the misty path on the western edge of Wistmead\tMarigold Boffin is on the western side of Wistmead, by the fog-enshrouded path that leads among the trees.\n6\tTalk to Marigold Boffin by the misty path out of Wistmead\tMarigold Boffin is on the western side of Wistmead, by the fog-enshrouded path that leads among the trees.\n7\tTravel the misty path through the woods west of Wistmead\tMarigold asked you to walk the foggy path west of Wistmead and then to report where it leads.\n8\tTalk to Marigold Boffin by the misty path out of Wistmead\tMarigold Boffin is on the western side of Wistmead, by the fog-enshrouded path that leads among the trees.\n9\tTalk to Bingo in Wistmead\tBingo is in Wistmead, near the eastern path that leads back to Hobbiton.\n",
[6453]="7004E17A\n1\tTalk to Dinodas in Wistmead\tDinodas is by the fire on the western side of Wistmead.\n2\tDinodas has reluctantly agreed to go with you along the misty path to the old Cleary farm. He suggested that you pick up the torch at his location and lead the way west along the mist-shrouded path into the forest.\t\n",
[6454]="7004E179\n1\tTravel to Wistmead and find Bingo\tA pony to Wistmead can be found to the east of the Party Tree.\n2\tHelp Bingo Boffin in Wistmead with 'Fun and Games?'\tBingo has asked to meet you at Wistmead, Walaric Goldworthy's new field of Harvest Festival fun.\n3\tHelp Bingo Boffin in Wistmead with 'The Parting Fog'\tBingo is in Wistmead, near the eastern path that leads back to Hobbiton.\n4\tHelp Bingo Boffin in Wistmead with 'The Haunting of Wistmead'\tBingo is in Wistmead, near the eastern path that leads back to Hobbiton.\n5\tHelp Bingo Boffin in Wistmead with 'None But One'\tBingo is in Wistmead, near the eastern path that leads back to Hobbiton.\n6\tTalk to Bingo in Wistmead\tBingo is in Wistmead, near the eastern path that leads back to Hobbiton.\n",
[6455]="7004E17B\n1\tTalk to Will Whitfoot in Michel Delving\tMayor Will Whitfoot is outside the Town Hole in Michel Delving, and may know something about Cleary's Acres.\n2\tTalk to Brombard Foxtail in Michel Delving\tBrombard Foxtail is the keeper of the Mathom-house, which stands on a rise overlooking the Town Hole in Michel Delving.\n3\tTalk to Postmaster Proudfoot in Michel Delving\tPostmaster Proudfoot is just outside the Quick Post, by the Town Hole in Michel Delving.\n4\tTalk to Postmaster Proudfoot and he will help you research the mystery of Cleary's Acres\tPostmaster Proudfoot is outside the Quick Post, near the Town Hole in Michel Delving.\n5\tTalk to Postmaster Proudfoot in Michel Delving\tPostmaster Proudfoot is outside the Quick Post, near the Town Hole in Michel Delving.\n6\tTalk to Clem Underhill, the Escrow Broker in Michel Delving\tClem Underhill is near the Town Hole in Michel Delving.\n7\tTalk to Bingo in Wistmead\tBingo is in Wistmead, near the eastern path from Hobbiton.\n",
[6456]="7004E17E\n1\tTalk to Walaric Goldworthy in Wistmead\tWalaric Goldworthy is in the field of Wistmead.\n2\tFind the location where Walaric Goldworthy moved some of the original fences and other debris found in Wistmead\tWalaric Goldworthy told you that you could see the junk-pile to the south-west, across the main path that runs through Wistmead.\n3\tExamine the junked wooden sign\tA face-down wooden sign lying among the debris of the junk-pile has caught your attention.\n4\tRead the newly-revealed writing on the discarded wooden sign\tA wooden sign lying among the debris of the junk-pile has caught your attention.\n5\tTalk to Bingo in Wistmead\tBingo is in Wistmead, near the eastern path that leads back to Hobbiton.\n6\tTalk to Walaric Goldworthy in Wistmead\tWalaric Goldworthy is in the field of Wistmead.\n7\tTalk to Bingo in Wistmead\tBingo is in Wistmead, near the eastern path that leads back to Hobbiton.\n",
[6457]="70017D87\n1\tPeer into the Reflecting Pool and revisit 'The Drowned Treasury'\tThe Reflecting Pool in the Twenty-first Hall of Moria will allow you to revisit 'The Drowned Treasury.' A Sage of Moria has challenged you to revisit the flooded depths of Ghân-gharâf. You can form a Fellowship to complete this quest with players currently on the original instance or on this Sage of Moria quest. All players will receive credit for completing the instance for their respective quests. NOTE: It is suggested that you complete this quest while in a fellowship. Inspiration will assist you if you choose to undertake this challenge alone or with a smaller group.\n2\tTalk to Rúnar\tRúnar, a Sage of Moria, can be found in the Twenty-first Hall of Moria. A Sage of Moria is waiting to speak with you about what you have learned by revisiting your adventures in the Drowned Treasury.\n",
[6458]="70017D88\n1\tPeer into the Reflecting Pool and revisit 'The Battle of the Deep-way'\tThe Reflecting Pool in the Twenty-first Hall of Moria will allow you to revisit 'The Battle of the Deep-way.' A Sage of Moria has challenged you to revisit the Battle of the Deep-way.\n2\tTalk to Rúnar\tRúnar, a Sage of Moria, can be found in the Twenty-first Hall of Moria. A Sage of Moria is waiting to speak with you about what you have learned by revisiting the Battle of the Deep-way.\n",
[6459]="70017D8A\n1\tPeer into the Reflecting Pool and revisit 'The Battle of the Twenty-first Hall'\tThe Reflecting Pool in the Twenty-first Hall of Moria will allow you to revisit 'The Battle of the Twenty-first Hall.' A Sage of Moria has challenged you to revisit your defence of the Twenty-first Hall.\n2\tTalk to Rúnar\tRúnar, a Sage of Moria, can be found in the Twenty-first Hall of Moria. A Sage of Moria is waiting to speak with you about what you have learned by revisiting your defence of the Twenty-first Hall.\n",
[6460]="70017D89\n1\tPeer into the Reflecting Pool and revisit 'The Battle of the Way of Smiths'\tThe Reflecting Pool in the Twenty-first Hall of Moria will allow you to revisit 'The Battle of the Way of Smiths.' A Sage of Moria has challenged you to revisit the Battle of the Way of Smiths.\n2\tTalk to Rúnar\tRúnar, a Sage of Moria, can be found in the Twenty-first Hall of Moria. A Sage of Moria is waiting to speak with you about what you have learned by revisiting your part of the Battle of the Way of Smiths.\n",
[6461]="70017D8B\n1\tPeer into the Reflecting Pool and revisit 'New Devilry'\tThe Reflecting Pool in the Twenty-first Hall of Moria will allow you to revisit 'New Devilry.' A Sage of Moria has challenged you to revisit the shadowy abyss of Azanarukâr. You can form a Fellowship to complete this quest with players currently on the original instance or on this Sage of Moria quest. All players will receive credit for completing the instance for their respective quests.\n2\tTalk to Rúnar\tRúnar, a Sage of Moria, can be found in the Twenty-first Hall of Moria. A Sage of Moria is waiting to speak with you about what you have learned by revisiting your adventures in Azanarukâr.\n",
[6462]="70046151\n1\tDeliver the ice block to the frozen sweet-cream stand\tThe ice block for delivery to Bywater can be found at the Party Tree. You should carry the ice to the frozen sweet-cream stand in Bywater.\n2\tSpeak with Bluet Goldworthy\tBluet Goldworthy is at her vendor stall in Bywater. You should speak with Bluet Goldworthy.\n",
[6463]="7000E76B\n1\tPlace the ice statuette at the shrine of the water-spirit\tThe Lossoth shrine lies along the shore of the Ice Bay, to the west and north of Pynti-peldot, past and downhill from the dwarf-make ruins known as the Lonesome Stones. Kimmo has asked you to find the Lossoth shrine to the water spirit and place the statuette on the pedestal there before it melts. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tTalk to Kimmo\tTell Kimmo back at Pynti-peldot that you have correctly placed the statuette.\n",
[6464]="7000A9E1\n1\tPresent an Icon of Heroes to Hróar at Gath Forthnír\030Craft an Icon of Heroes (quantity: see journal)\tHróar is at Gath Forthnír in Angmar. Hróar has asked you to craft an Icon of Heroes and bring it to him.\n",
})
